  "enhanced_information": "For the contraction of striated muscle fibers, Ca2+ binds to Troponin, causing a conformational change in tropomyosin, which allows myosin-actin interaction and muscle contraction. This is supported by the consensus that Ca2+ binding to Troponin leads to the exposure of myosin-binding sites on actin, initiating muscle contraction. Relevant evidence paths confirm the interaction of Troponin with muscle fibers and tropomyosin, further supporting the role of Ca2+ in muscle contraction."
